WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/driving/components/drive-detail/RouteMapSection.tsx + the geometry its parent
  useDriveDetailData.ts computes:
    FadeIn → GlassPanel(overflow-hidden) →
      header  : <MapPin/> + t('driveDetail.route','Route')
      if trail.length>0:
        Leaflet map (MapLayerSwitcher, MapTileLayer, MapInvalidator, FitBounds=useMap):
          hasRoute (hasMeaningfulRoute(positions) — ≥2 valid coords ≥10 m apart):
            speedSegments polylines coloured by per-point SI m/s band
              (#10b981 <30mph · #00f0ff 30–60 · #f59e0b 60–100 · #ef4444 >100 ; *0.44704 SI)
            start CircleMarker (green) Popup[start + formatDateTime]
            end   CircleMarker (red)   Popup[end   + (endTs ? formatDateTime : 'In progress')]
          !hasRoute (stationary GPS): anchor CircleMarker (cyan, 'Last known location')
                                      + AlertBanner('Route can't be plotted' / stationary body)
        footer  : Start:<formatTime>  |  legend(4 bands→display unit via convertSpeedFromSI+fmtNumber
                  + unit) when hasRoute&&trail>1  |  End:<formatTime> (when endTs)
      else: empty — <MapPin/> + t('driveDetail.noRouteData','No route data available for this drive')
  Data sources (web hooks): useMap (Leaflet camera → MapKit camera), useTranslation (i18n facade),
                            useUnits (speed unit + convertSpeedFromSI). Route data arrives as props the
                            parent page derives from the DriveDetail DTO — reproduced from a DTO here.
  i18n keys (verbatim from source): driveDetail.{route,start,end,inProgress,lastKnown,
                                    stationaryRouteTitle,stationaryRouteBody,noRouteData}.

